  "memo": "Glossy Privet is used extensively as a shrub or tree standard. It is tough and durable, and its dark shiny green foliage makes it desirable. The showy white flower clusters are attractive, however, the odor may be objectionable. The profusion of berries afterward are not especially attractive and can be messy. It reseeds freely and is drought tolerant. It takes shearing. It often requires regularly scheduled light top-trimming (but not necessarily shearing) of vigorous top shoots to maintain a lower height.",
